#: ../../source/guides/engine/conventions/index.rst:3
msgid "Conventions and house style"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/engine/conventions/index.rst:7
msgid ""
"**These are conventions, not rules, and their only purpose is "
"consistency.** They are what this codebase happens to have settled on, "
"written down so that a reader can predict the next file before opening it"
" and a contributor does not have to guess. Almost every one of them is "
"*arbitrary* — a coin-toss between defensible options that was worth "
"deciding once so nobody has to decide it again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/engine/conventions/index.rst:13
msgid ""
"So: follow them where they help, and say so where they do not. A "
"convention that makes your change worse is a convention with a missing "
"exception, and pointing that out is more useful than complying. What "
"genuinely matters is much shorter than what follows — that the tests are "
"honest, that errors are not silently swallowed, and that the next person "
"can read what you wrote. The rest is house style, and house style is "
"negotiable."
msgstr ""

